<DocsLayout
  title="AI Providers & Speech Models"
  description="Use your own cloud API key, run locally with Ollama, and configure local or GPU speech recognition."
  currentPath="/docs/ai-providers"
  section="AI Providers & ASR"
>
  <h2>Supported AI Providers</h2>
  <p>
    Configure your AI provider in <strong>Settings → AI</strong> or in <code>.env</code> via{" "}
    <code>CLIPCUT_AI_PROVIDER</code>, <code>CLIPCUT_AI_MODELS</code>, and{" "}
    <code>CLIPCUT_AI_KEY</code>. Dashboard settings override <code>.env</code>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>gemini</code> — Google Gemini (e.g. <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code>)</li>
    <li><code>openai</code> — OpenAI (e.g. <code>gpt-4o-mini</code>)</li>
    <li><code>xai</code> — xAI Grok (e.g. <code>grok-4</code>)</li>
    <li><code>groq</code> — Groq (e.g. <code>llama-3.3-70b-versatile</code>)</li>
    <li><code>openrouter</code> — OpenRouter (any listed model ID)</li>
    <li><code>anthropic</code> — Anthropic Claude</li>
    <li><code>ollama</code> — Local Ollama (no API key, e.g. <code>llama3.1</code>)</li>
    <li><code>custom</code> — Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint via <code>CLIPCUT_AI_BASE_URL</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Without an AI key, ClipCut still works automatically by picking the loudest moments that
    contain speech.
  </p>

  <h2>Speech Recognition (ASR)</h2>
  <p>
    ClipCut checks YouTube transcripts first when <code>CLIPCUT_YT_TRANSCRIPT=1</code>, then uses{" "}
    <code>faster-whisper</code> as its single default multi-language speech-to-text model (handling
    automatic language detection and 99+ languages), plus Hindi/Urdu Romanized captions.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
